modern_restatement_en:
Let $C=F_m\cap G_n\subset\mathbb P^3$ be a general complete intersection of surfaces of degrees $m,n$, so $\deg C=mn$. Determine the degrees of three ruled surfaces associated with $C$:
(a) the tangent developable, whose degree is the rank $mn(m+n-2)$;
(b) the surface of principal normals;
(c) the surface of the 'axes of the osculating planes', i.e. binormals or polar lines.
The surfaces in (b) and (c) are metric: they depend on the absolute conic.
